
# 2026-03-27 07:03:23.649799
+BUG DESCRIPTION --------------- Actual Behavior: The system throws or displays an error when a requested item does not exist. The system also throws or displays an error when an item exists but its quantity is 0. When deleting an object, the client does not receive a clear success response or confirmation. Expected Behavior: When an item does not exist, the API should return a 404 Not Found with a clear JSON error body and the frontend should show a friendly 'Item not found' message without throwing. When an item has quantity 0, the API should return 200 with quantity: 0 and an explicit out-of-stock indicator so the frontend can render an out-of-stock state without errors. When deleting an item, the API should return a definitive success response (200 with {'success': true} or 204) and the frontend should display a confirmation. Affected Area: Inventory/item retrieval and deletion endpoints and the frontend item detail/delete flows. ASSUMPTIONS ----------- - ⚠️ The errors reported are coming from the backend API endpoints (GET /items/{id}, DELETE /items/{id}) and not purely client-side validation. - ⚠️ The delete endpoint currently returns an unexpected status or empty response that the frontend does not interpret as success. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA ------------------- 1. Given an item ID that does not exist, when a client requests GET /items/{id}, then the API responds with HTTP 404 and a JSON body containing {'error': 'Item not found'} and the frontend displays a non-error 'Item not found' message without exceptions. 2. Given an item exists with quantity 0, when a client requests GET /items/{id}, then the API responds with HTTP 200 and a body that includes 'quantity': 0 and 'status': 'out_of_stock', and the frontend renders an out-of-stock state without throwing errors. 3. No regression in item listing and update flows.
+
+  Instructions:
+  - Read the repo map and find the relevant files yourself.
+  - Make the minimal, targeted change needed.
+  - Do not refactor unrelated code.
+  - Do not create new files unless necessary.
+  

